= installation

./configure.sh && make && ./deploy.sh

If at any step a command fails, investigate and try again.

configure doesn't actually configure anything; it
just whines if you don't have something installed.
maybe it should generate the Makefile's build
date/versions if i get to it later, i don't know.

To uninstall i imagine something like this will do:

git clean -fx ; rm -rf /usr/local/opt/homebox*

To *just* build the backend because JavaScript is a
ginormous memory-hog:

make build-backend && ...

(Also in case that annoying "JS heap OOM" shows up,
export one of these for subprocesses to see:

NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=2048"
NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=4096"
NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=8192"

Don't worry things probably won't crash :'D)
